SHN FHIR validator image
========================

This image is the FHIR $validate sidecar of the SHN Smart Gateway. Its source is the
`deploy/validator/` directory of https://github.com/SmartHealthNetwork/shn-gateway.
The parts SHN wrote are licensed under the Apache License 2.0
(`third-party-licenses/Apache-2.0.txt`). This directory is `/licenses/` in the image.

What the image contains, and under which terms
----------------------------------------------

1. Base layers: `gcr.io/distroless/java21-debian13:nonroot`, pinned by digest, the
   base the `hapiproject/hapi` image is built on. Nothing in it changes; the image adds
   only the files items 2 to 4 name and this directory. It is a distroless Debian base
   with the Eclipse Temurin 21 Java runtime (GPLv2 with the Classpath Exception).
   Each Debian package's copyright file is under `/usr/share/doc/` in the image, and
   the Java runtime's own notices are in its `legal/` directory under `/usr/lib/jvm/`.
   Corresponding source: Debian at https://sources.debian.org and Temurin at
   https://adoptium.net.

2. The HAPI FHIR JPA server (`/app/main.war`, Apache-2.0). One class is changed:
   `org.hl7.fhir.common.hapi.validation.validator.ValidatorWrapper`, in the
   `hapi-fhir-validation` 8.12.0 jar inside the WAR, is rebuilt from its upstream
   source with a change applied, under Apache-2.0 like the upstream class. The change,
   its source and its build are in `deploy/validator/backport/` of the source
   repository, and `/app/backport-provenance.json` records the upstream and rebuilt
   artifacts' digests. `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` beside this file lists the third-party
   libraries inside the WAR that need a notice, and says which those are. HAPI's own
   jars carry HL7's terminology package (`hl7.terminology`, CC0-1.0) as HL7 publishes
   it, including a fragment of SNODENT (166 concepts; SNODENT is the American Dental
   Association's) and code system definitions for other systems without their content.

3. `/healthcheck`: the validator's supervisor and readiness probe, written by SHN
   (Apache-2.0) and built with the Go standard library (BSD-3-Clause,
   `Go-LICENSE.txt`).

4. FHIR packages in `/packages/`, shipped byte-for-byte as published:
   - HL7 implementation guide packages (US Core, Da Vinci CRD, DTR, PAS, PDex, CDex,
     HRex, SDC and, on the 2.2 line, the R4 extensions pack), from
     packages.simplifier.net, each released by HL7 under CC0-1.0. Terminology from
     other code systems that they carry stays under its owners' terms (see
     "Terminology" below).
   - `shn.fhir.carry`, written by SHN (Apache-2.0).
   - `shn.fhir.validation-support`, assembled by SHN (Apache-2.0). It carries the
     HCPCS Level II and Place of Service code systems, built from the Centers for
     Medicare & Medicaid Services' public files, and resources copied unchanged from
     HL7's `hl7.fhir.uv.xver-r5.r4` 0.1.0 and `hl7.fhir.uv.extensions.r4`
     5.3.0-ballot-tc1 packages (CC0-1.0).

Terminology
-----------

The HL7 packages, in `/packages/` and inside HAPI's own jars, carry content from
other code systems, which stays under its owners' terms:

- This material contains content from LOINC (http://loinc.org). LOINC is copyright
  © Regenstrief Institute, Inc. and the Logical Observation Identifiers Names and
  Codes (LOINC) Committee and is available at no cost under the license at
  http://loinc.org/license. LOINC® is a registered United States trademark of
  Regenstrief Institute, Inc.
- SNOMED CT content is copyright SNOMED International. HL7 distributes it under its
  agreement with SNOMED International; using SNOMED CT in your own systems requires
  a licence from SNOMED International or its member in your country.

No CPT code set, and no value set that lists CPT codes, is included. Individual CPT
codes appear only as examples, a few with display text: inside HL7's packages, and in
the supervisor's synthetic self-test fixtures. CPT is a registered trademark of the
American Medical Association.

No X12 code lists are included. Individual X12 code values appear only as examples,
inside HL7's packages and in the supervisor's synthetic self-test fixtures.

No CDT (dental procedure) codes are included.
